course: dictionary
lesson: 9059
title: A word that lives in a phrase
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sleight is a word you will nearly always find in a special phrase: sleight of hand. Do not try to work out sleight on its own. Read the whole phrase together, and look at the words around it.
explain: «Magicians use sleight of hand (quick hand tricks) and misdirection (making you look away from the trick) to fool the senses on purpose.» The brackets are clues. Sleight of hand means quick hand tricks, and misdirection is a different idea, explained straight away.
explain: «Sleight of hand is quick, practised hand movement you don't notice.» Practised means done again and again until you are very good at it. So sleight means a clever, quick skill with the hands. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "clever, quick hand movement you don't notice" still makes sense.
fact: Sleight means a clever, quick skill, especially with the hands.
fact: «Sleight of hand» means quick, practised hand movements that people do not notice.
fact: Magicians use sleight of hand to make a coin seem to vanish.
fact: Sleight of hand fools our eyes, because we do not see the secret move.
fact: Tricksters can use sleight of hand in games like "find the lady" to cheat people.
exercise: «Sleight of hand means quick, practised hand movements you do not notice.» What is sleight of hand? | A way to draw very straight lines | *Quick hand movements that people do not notice | A loud shout across the room | A kind of slow dance
exercise: A magician makes a coin seem to vanish. What skill is he using? | Swimming | *Sleight of hand | Singing | Counting coins out loud
exercise: Which two words usually come after sleight in this lesson? | of day | *of hand | of mind | of word
test: «Magicians use sleight of hand and misdirection to fool the senses on purpose.» What does misdirection mean in this sentence? | Fooling the magician himself | A kind of sleight | *Making you look away from the trick | Hand tricks that you can see
test: A trickster in a park game cheats a crowd with quick, unseen hand moves. Which word fits best? | Ancient | *Sleight | Barely | Glum
exam: Which best describes sleight? | *A clever, quick skill with the hands | A kind of map | A loud, sudden noise | A slow, careful movement
